  "description": "This easy salad combines sweet Medjool dates, bitter radicchio, crunchy cucumbers, fresh mint, and a spicy tahini-yogurt dressing for a bold, crunchy dish that's company-worthy but easy enough for weeknights.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: 1 teaspoon orange blossom water (optional)\n\nOptional substitutions: gochujang → sriracha or harissa\n\nNotes: I prefer gochujang in this salad for its savory-sweet depth; for a brighter, more vinegary heat, use sriracha, and for a smokier, more complex heat, use harissa.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The dressing can be prepared up to 4 days in advance and refrigerated in an airtight container. Loosen with water as needed before serving.\nThe dates can be macerated and refrigerated in an airtight container up to 1 day in advance.",
